                <pb facs="0914" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.48 Earthquake of 1931/80: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1931-04-06T13:30:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1931-04-05T15:00:00-05:45">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        April 6, 1931—1:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Supplementing my [April] 4th, 8 p.m. Major R. J. Mitchell commanding aircraft
                    forces of the Marine Brigade here commends highly the cooperation given by
                    planes of the Pan American Airways in the evacuation of wives and families of
                    American officers from Managua and urges that appropriate acknowledgment of this
                    cooperation be made to Mr. Trippe. Major Mitchell specially mentions the
                    splendid work of Messrs. E. Balluder, D. D. Richardson, H. B. Lewis, W. L.
                    Morrison, H. Rammer, R. E. Frizell, Archie Paschal, and J. Dymond.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
